  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">INCLUSIVE COMMUNITIES: INCREASING ACCESS TO RIGHTS AND PARTICIPATION OF PEOPLE WITH DISABILITIES ON PERSONAL, COMMUNITY AND SOCIETAL LEVELS, IN KENYA</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Inclusive Communities will increase access to rights and participation of people with disabilities on personal, community and societal levels, in Kenya and Zimbabwe. There is a particular focus on women, girls and people with mental health and psychosocial disabilities &#x2013; those who can be the most vulnerable &#x2013; through our Community Mental Health Approach (CMH). It will strengthen organisations of people with disabilities (OPDs) capacity to raise awareness, reduce disability stigma and advocate for systemic change. It will improve access to education, peer support, health services and livelihood opportunities through community-based inclusive development (CBID), improving resilience at individual and community level.</narrative>
  </description>
